   100	
   101	*Officer.* He wrote his name and grade.
   102	
   103	*Present duty.* He wrote it as his order had it: *Records, junior chair, institutional proceedings at Ostrand; the seat's Fifth-days, until relieved.*
   104	
   105	*Relief sought upon.* He considered that for some time, and wrote *The conclusion of the proceedings by ruling.* It was tomorrow, and a man might fairly ask to be relieved of a duty on the day the duty ended.
   106	
   107	*Posting sought.* The district seat's records room was a man short. He had seen it for himself when he went there with a rubbing of a seal: an impression book four months behind, and a ledger of dies that nobody had balanced against the cutters' copies since the last officer left. He wrote *District records, Ostrand, or any records room that is short.* He did not write *out of monitoring*, for the form had no line for what a man wished to leave.
