   153	"It said Iron," said Lira. She had got her breath. "I was on the bench by the door and I watched the middle assessor's face when the plate came up. He looked like a man who'd put his hand in his pocket for a coin and found the coin he expected." She shoved her hands deeper into her own pockets. "He was right about himself, in front of people whose job it was to check. I saw it happen. I wanted somebody to have seen it who knew what it was."
