   155	Brom did not say anything to that. He stood in the market street with his forearms marked and his face quite calm, and Cael saw that it had been enough. Whatever a clerk wrote on whatever paper, a plate had come up warm under his boots and said what was so.
   156	
   157	"The hour after noon," said Bracken, and put the card away. "I suggest that everybody eats."
