   194	
   195	What he felt was not the floor going. It was a corridor ending. He had been walking down it so long that he had stopped feeling the walls, and now there was a last door, with a year's close chalked on it, and behind him nothing whatever that he needed to go back for.
   196	
   197	The seat rose. It gathered its one leaf, and turned, and went to its own door, and for a moment the grey back was all there was of it. He had tried at fourteen sittings to learn something from how that shape sat, and had wanted a face under it, because a face could be read, and hated, and found out.
