   252	
   253	"So it's honest."
   254	
   255	"It is exactly what it says it is. There is nothing behind it at all." He said it in his mild voice, as he might have reported a floor schedule. "In my trade a man is taught four grades of pressure, in their order. The record. The instrument. The knock, which is paper nobody will own. And last the hand, which is a road with no paper at all. I was taught that the hand was the worst of them, and I believed it for fifteen years." He shook his head, very slightly. "I had the order wrong. What stood in the road was a glove." He looked down at the last line of the leaf. "*Given under the Compact's hand.* That is the only true sentence of its kind I have been shown this year. This is the hand. It does not have another."
