   257	He squared the leaf to the counter's edge, and stepped back from it.
   258	
   259	"I am sorry," he said. "I should have liked to find something. It would have been easier for you."
   260	
   261	Cael looked at the engrossment under the lamp.
   262	
   263	*I keep looking for the person and finding the hand.* That was his own line, from the year's sixth week, and he had gone on looking, at Jent and at a hood and down a road with chalk on it. He stopped looking. It was like setting down a thing he had carried so long that he had forgotten it had weight.
