editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:550:The lamp had burned down to a blue bead before anybody moved. Karis and Lira fell into an argument about next year's tournament, and the qualifying rules, on a point that neither of them had the papers for. Karis quoted articles. Lira, who never wrote anything down, recited the closing standings of the last three Copper seasons from memory, top line to bottom, to win it, and won it. Brom told Karis that she could not possibly be right about something, and was asked what, and could not remember what, and the two of them laughed until Karis had to put her head down on the table.
